  "question": {
    "text": "The gas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>'</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>'</mo></math> is having very low reactivity reaches to stratosphere. It is non-toxic and non-flammable but dissociated by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>UV</mi></math>-radiations in stratosphere. The intermediates formed initially from the gas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>'</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>'</mo></math> are:",
